==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
When the stage starts, you will be able to stall with [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong cat]] and [[Weedwacker Cat|Weedwacker Cat]] for some money, bringing anti-Dark units is recommended to defeat the Shadow Boxer K without high levels, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] in particular is good, but any decent anti-Dark can work. Combining your anti-Dark of choice with a spammable ranged area attacker such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg cat]] will make this level a breeze. Utilizing [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed/Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] is recommended for supporting damage.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
You have plenty of time to save up cat worker levels so use that to your advantage. The peons aren't worth very much but you can save as long as you want to. However, a similar strategy to Chapter 1's outbreak should net you the win.

When you attack the enemy base the trio of Roos spawn to fight you. The Zang Roo will burrow past your meatshields, leaving your backlines to get torn up unless you spawn protective units at just the right time. Shigong Cat especially excels due to the amount of punishment they can take from Zombie enemies.

Just when you think you've won, a second wave will spawn to ruin your day. Tackle them the same way as last time, just careful of the burrow and the 100% revive of Zang Roo and you'll be just fine.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The stage is quite tame until you hit the base so getting to level 4 worker cat and spawning a few expensive Units is not a problem.

Once you do hit the base, everything else comes right at you including the Li'l Zyclone to block off your meatshield support. Zang Roo is replaced by Zuche, who immediately burrows and starts to destroy your ubers if you aren't spawning enough Meatshields. Scissoroo and Shadow Boxer K are going to make quick work of your most forward meatshields so just be prepared for the double burrow with constant meatshielding and spawning something to help as soon as the bosswave hits you.

This is an all out slug fest where timing is super crucial. As always, as many [[Zombie Killer|Zombie Killers]] and treasures as possible are recommended to smooth out the stage but you still may have to retry a couple time, Li'l Zyclone is no joke and he can easily keep your meatshields from getting to the front line, costing you your entire team of Ubers if you're not careful.

Li'l Zyclone is not a Floating enemy so you'll want your trusty Weedwacker or [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight]] to help slow him down. Shadow Boxer K and Scissoroo are big parts of the stage so if they're giving you trouble add some more anti-Alien/Black cats to your roster. Pizza Cat is a reliable choice for defeating the Shadow Boxer Ks.

